MANACHER’S ALGORITHM
(Longest Palindromic Substring in O(N))

This is a rare but powerful algorithm. If you explain this well, interviewers know you’re strong in DSA.

1️⃣ Problem Statement

Given a string s, find the longest palindromic substring in linear time.

📌 A palindrome reads the same forwards and backwards.

Example
Input  : "babad"
Output : "bab"   (or "aba")

2️⃣ Why Not Brute Force?
Approach	Time
Check all substrings	O(N³) ❌
Expand Around Center	O(N²) ❌
Manacher’s Algorithm	O(N) ✅
3️⃣ Key Idea (Intuition)

Manacher’s Algorithm:

Handles odd & even length palindromes together

Uses previous palindrome information

Avoids re-checking characters

4️⃣ Preprocessing the String (VERY IMPORTANT)

Insert # between characters to make all palindromes odd-length.

Example
Original:  b a b a d
Modified: #b#a#b#a#d#


This simplifies logic.

5️⃣ Key Arrays Used
Variable	Meaning
P[i]	Palindrome radius centered at i
C	Center of current palindrome
R	Right boundary of current palindrome
6️⃣ Algorithm (Step-by-Step)

Transform input string

Initialize array P[]

Loop through transformed string

Use mirror property to reduce comparisons

Expand palindrome when possible

Update center and right boundary

Extract longest palindrome from P[]

7️⃣ Java Code (Clean & Explained)
class Manacher {

    public static String longestPalindrome(String s) {

        // Step 1: Transform string
        StringBuilder t = new StringBuilder("#");
        for (char c : s.toCharArray()) {
            t.append(c).append("#");
        }

        int n = t.length();
        int[] P = new int[n];

        int C = 0, R = 0;
        int maxLen = 0, centerIndex = 0;

        // Step 2: Main loop
        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {

            int mirror = 2 * C - i;

            if (i < R) {
                P[i] = Math.min(R - i, P[mirror]);
            }

            // Expand palindrome
            int a = i + P[i] + 1;
            int b = i - P[i] - 1;

            while (a < n && b >= 0 &&
                   t.charAt(a) == t.charAt(b)) {
                P[i]++;
                a++;
                b--;
            }

            // Update center and boundary
            if (i + P[i] > R) {
                C = i;
                R = i + P[i];
            }

            // Track longest palindrome
            if (P[i] > maxLen) {
                maxLen = P[i];
                centerIndex = i;
            }
        }

        // Step 3: Extract result
        int start =
            (centerIndex - maxLen) / 2;
        return s.substring(start,
                            start + maxLen);
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        System.out.println(
            longestPalindrome("babad"));
    }
}

8️⃣ Line-by-Line Explanation
🔹 String Transformation
#b#a#b#a#d#


Uniform handling of even & odd palindromes

🔹 Mirror Logic
int mirror = 2 * C - i;


Uses symmetry of palindrome

Reduces comparisons

🔹 Expansion Logic
while (t.charAt(a) == t.charAt(b))


Grow palindrome outward

🔹 Update Center
if (i + P[i] > R)


Expand window when palindrome grows larger

